## Visual concept used

A **master instrument cluster wired to an annual block-cycle dial** — the "whole machine, assembled" synthesis poster, and deliberately the fullest, busiest instrument in the Fit set. **Zone 1** is the hero: four labeled gauge banks (CHASSIS cyan / ENGINE amber / OUTPUTS violet / CONTROL teal) carrying all 17 benchmarks as `target ▸ you ▸ gap` horizontal gauges, each with an authoritative red **redline** tick and a "you" needle stopped short of it — the visible gap is the diagnosis, not a pass/fail check (the explicit thing §7 says to avoid). A 2×2 bank grid with a legend + honest-timeline pin ("2–3 yrs of intelligent work") tucked into the short-bank gaps, and the "gaps are the diagnosis" caption under the whole cluster. **Zone 2** is a four-sector annular **block-cycle dial** — Q1 FOUNDATION illuminated as **BUILD**, Q2/Q3/Q4 dimmed to **HOLD** with faint domain tints, a rotation arrow on the rim and a "BUILD ONE · HOLD THE REST · SWAP" hub — paired with a right-hand readout listing what each quarter builds vs holds. **Zone 3** is the calm "maintenance idle" meter (HOLD THE WHOLE PANEL ≈ 3–4 hrs/wk, near-idle gauge) + the "build hard once, then hold easily, for decades" deal box. A quiet two-line **dividend footer** closes it (LONGEVITY — Mandsager 2018, n=122,007, no upper limit; AVAILABILITY — a body that does what you ask). Semantic color rationed: green reserved for the maintenance-idle payoff, red reserved for the redline ticks only; the four domain accents read as one family. Locked **Engineering Diagnostic Instrument** style; a new sub-archetype distinct from 2.0 (signal trace), 3.0 (fault splitter), 3.2 (assembly), 4.0 (interference scope).

